This implementation independently authors the JACS instructions, corpus observations,
scripts, and synthetic evaluation examples; it does not bundle upstream skills.

Journal policies are linked to ACS primary sources. Article metadata and source locators
identify the original publications; this project's license does not relicense those papers.
No ACS endorsement or affiliation is implied.

Figure source discovery and local inspection use the PubMed Central Article Dataset,
provided by the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM), and associated Europe PMC records.
https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/tools/pmcaws/
The public registry records each source's DOI, version, license code, URL and digest.
Original article text and figure images are not redistributed in this repository.
Public figure observations are independently written descriptions; demonstration artwork
and evaluation datasets are original, synthetic examples, not scientific research results.

Design workflow inspiration for v0.3:
OpenAI Data plugin (data-analytics 1.0.8), visualize-data and validate-data skills,
and its shared analysis-quality instructions. The relationship-first chart selection,
population/scale checks, semantic encodings and rendered-artifact review are independently
adapted here; this repository does not redistribute the plugin or claim its endorsement.

Writing workflow adaptation for v0.7:
Data 1.0.8 analysis-quality criteria inform metric/population reconciliation, independent
arithmetic checks and the separation of observed advantages from causal interpretations.
The writing guidance and synthetic exercises are independently authored. Private paired
manuscript revisions used for editorial learning are not redistributed.

Optional color-vision previews use Colorspacious and its Machado et al. model implementation:
https://colorspacious.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorial.html
These modeled previews do not certify universal accessibility or visual comfort.
